1
00:00:00,414 --> 00:00:06,322
At noon, witnesses reported a bell
sounding from a tower built without one.

2
00:00:06,598 --> 00:00:12,962
The mounting frame stood empty, with no bell
or other sound-making instrument in view.

3
00:00:13,238 --> 00:00:20,511
The event is clear in outline: a reported sound,
an empty frame, and an unidentified source.

4
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:23,587
That unanswered contrast begins the case.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,455
Clock repairer Mira Vale follows the
evidence because her brother is missing.

6
00:00:32,978 --> 00:00:38,886
A note attributed to him was left
among the materials on her workbench.

7
00:00:40,408 --> 00:00:46,772
Beside it rests a brass moth, a small
object whose purpose is still unknown.

8
00:00:48,294 --> 00:00:55,112
Clocks and records repeat nine seventeen, bringing
the note, moth, and time into one sequence.

9
00:00:56,634 --> 00:01:02,998
Together they form a trail of clues,
though not a map to her brother.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,455
The note leads Mira to a ledger
divided into two facing columns.

11
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:18,758
One column records minutes; the
other records people's names.

12
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:26,425
The visible pages establish those two categories,
while their purpose remains unresolved.

13
00:01:28,637 --> 00:01:35,001
Their relationship to the missing brother
is a question the case has not answered.

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,364
From the ledger, the investigation turns
toward the city council indicated by the note.

15
00:01:48,849 --> 00:01:55,667
The note makes the council relevant, but remains
an allegation rather than proof of involvement.

16
00:01:59,152 --> 00:02:03,243
The ledger's origin and authenticity
are also open questions.

17
00:02:06,728 --> 00:02:14,001
So the council, the ledger, and the tower occupy
the same investigation without a proven mechanism.

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,727
What is established is the evidence set: reported bell,
empty frame, note, brass moth, nine seventeen, ledger.

19
00:02:27,204 --> 00:02:34,022
The ledger visibly separates minutes from names, but
the significance of those categories remains uncertain.

20
00:02:35,499 --> 00:02:41,863
The source of the sound and the location
of Mira's brother are still unknown.

21
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:48,795
Any connection between the council and the
collected evidence is likewise unresolved.

22
00:02:50,272 --> 00:02:57,999
For now, the tower remains an open case,
defined as much by its limits as its clues.
